# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# GitHub reads this to offer a "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo and
# similar archives read it for author and licence metadata. R2 in
# docs/launch-tickets.md asks for it so the work is citable.
#
# `version` is held to package.json and the changelog by
# tests/documentation.test.ts: a citation naming a version that was never
# released is the kind of wrong nobody notices until somebody cites it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BankLang: a deterministic compiler from BankTS to IBM Enterprise COBOL"
message: "If you refer to this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hassan
    alias: MWH997
    email: mwh007@outlook.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/MWH997/banklang"
url: "https://banklang.mwhassan.com"
abstract: >-
  BankLang compiles BankTS, a deliberately small TypeScript-like language for
  banking logic, to readable IBM Enterprise COBOL, a copybook for every record,
  and the JCL to build and run it. Compilation is deterministic: no model
  decides what is generated, and the same input always produces byte-identical
  output. The compiler refuses to compile financially unsafe programs —
  unbalanced ledger postings, retries with no idempotency key, and money
  movement with no audit trail are compile errors rather than review comments.
  Generated COBOL is validated locally with GnuCOBOL; no IBM Enterprise COBOL
  validation is claimed.
keywords:
  - COBOL
  - IBM Enterprise COBOL
  - mainframe
  - z/OS
  - compiler
  - banking
  - CICS
  - Db2
  - JCL
license: MIT
version: 0.9.0
